Lobium — register the //components/lobium_fp config-channel module in the build graph.

Wires the added first-party module (components/lobium_fp/, staged by lobium/build.sh) into the two Blink
targets whose hooks read lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current():
  - blink core (component("core")):  deps += //components/lobium_fp ; core/DEPS += +components/lobium_fp
  - blink common (source_set("common")): deps += //components/lobium_fp ; common/DEPS += +components/lobium_fp
    (blink_common owns approximated_device_memory.cc — the deviceMemory single source).

Kept minimal, and in the //components first-party root rather than //third_party (which the license
scanner tools/licenses.py rejects for a directory lacking README.chromium/LICENSE, breaking the
is_official_build credits step). COMPILE-VERIFIED on Chromium 152.0.7928.0.

